WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.917 --> 00:00:04.963
Who do you trust with
your deepest hurts,

00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:08.508
your most painful truths?

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.844
And what will you do
if you found out

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:14.973
that your most trusted
ally was lying to you?

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:18.059
(dramatic music)

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:21.271
This season, Poppy
is experiencing things

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:24.482
still residual from season one.

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:26.276
It's her personal life

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:29.696
that is a part of
the case itself

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.197
that needs to be solved.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.284
All of Poppy's personal
relationships

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:38.580
are being affected by her
needing to deal

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:41.791
with what is damaging her.

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:45.128
Everyone's dealing
with something

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:47.255
that they're carrying
in their life

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:48.590
that's either holding them back

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.425
or has held them back

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:53.553
or that they're still
deeply struggling with.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.471
(dramatic music)

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:55.972
People are drawn to people
with flaws.

00:00:55.972 --> 00:00:57.974
Drama is about imperfection.

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:00.685
Something's perfect,
then who cares, right?

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:02.312
It's the moments in between.

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:05.398
The damaged people
are so delicious

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.609
and it's so much fun
to watch them

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.403
as they dig inside and
grapple with their truth.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.446
(sirens wailing)

00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:13.615
There's no one that is
unscathed by

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:16.284
humanity and earth and
the world that itself.

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:18.328
I think people really can

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:20.830
delve into who these
characters are.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.333
You can relate to the pain
of the damage

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:26.836
that's been inflicted
upon that person.

00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:30.131
There's a lot that we're
dealing with on this show.

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:32.592
A lot of, lot of conflicts.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.303
(dramatic music)

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.601
(screaming)

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.146
In trying to find out
what happened to Joshua,

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:47.357
we find out more about
this deep love

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:49.776
that these women have
for each other,

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.154
that's also hiding
a lot of secrets.

00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:54.656
(dramatic music)

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:58.034
It's a very complex
world that Michelle's created,

00:01:58.034 --> 00:02:00.620
but a really beautiful
one, really textured one.

00:02:01.913 --> 00:02:03.164
There are no heroes

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:04.958
and that's what makes them real.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.334
And that's what makes them
interesting.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:10.797
I knew better than to
expect anything from anyone.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.675
The beauty of what it means
to find those very difficult,

00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:17.387
emotional, deep layers that not
only are in the writing,

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:19.389
but also within myself.

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:20.515
(dramatic music)

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:23.143
It's all about what's
underneath.

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:26.688
We are constantly forcing
each other to be truthful

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:29.190
and we're always holding back.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:32.610
When we don't deal with
our childhood traumas,

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.906
they do become the demons that
hold us hostage as adults.

00:02:36.906 --> 00:02:38.408
I love you Micah.

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.534
I love you too.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.327
I don't think she's afraid

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.122
what she'll discover
about Micah,

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:47.250
I think she's more afraid
of what she'll discover about

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.209
herself.

00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:51.296
(dramatic music)

